                "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please push changes to the relation chain / topic showing how it helps upstream configurations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "+1, would like to see a real-life use case"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "on many server platforms, there can be multiple instances of same fru each are uniquely identified by the instance numbers. To keep the stable instance number that can be reused across all related objects for that FRU, we need to extract numeric token from it's name.\n\nHaving such a property which tells the instance number/slotnumber, it makes it possible to seamlessly correlate inventory objects with LEDs, sensors, Redfish resources, etc., thus providing consistent dbus object naming.\n\neg:\n    \"Exposes\": [\n        {\n            \"Address\": \"$address\",\n            \"Bus\": \"$bus\",\n            \"Name\": \"PCIe Card 0\",\n            \"Type\": \"EEPROM\",\n            \"InstanceNumber\": \"@Name\" => Created a new dbus property (InstanceNumber = 0)\n        }\n     ]\n\nThe newly created property can be used to create other related objects for that FRU. eg:\n/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/chassis/assembly/pcie_card3\n  \u251c\u2500 maps to \u2192 /xyz/openbmc_project/led/pcie3\n  \u251c\u2500 maps to \u2192 /xyz/openbmc_project/temp/pcie3\n  \u251c\u2500 maps to \u2192 /redfish/v1/Chassis/HGX_GPU_3"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I would suggest to make a full example using at least a full configuration record with Name, Type, ..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "```suggestion\nEg:\nIf the config json contains:\n\"DeviceName\": \"PCIe SLOT @{SlotNumber}\"\n\"SlotNumber\": \"6\"\n```\n\nReplacing it the other way around would be simpler for the example use-case since there is no need to extract a number."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "When doing any kind of template var, please provide a boundary like `@{DeviceName}`.\n\nThe current template var system like `$bus` has a huge problem because there is no clear end to the template var."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "No need to do the other way around as it's already achieved by using the existing $ symbol.\n\"DeviceName\": \"PCIe SLOT $SlotNumber\" => will do the same"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "In entity manager config jsons, the property name is followed in pascal case without any spaces, which itself sets a clear end. so I would suggest to keep it the same way for @ or any other new commands to make it consistent."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> to make it consistent.\n\nstep 1: create broken template var system\nstep 2: not merge @chaul@amperecomputing.com 's fix for said template system\nstep 3: re-use the broken idea to create new template var system\n\nYou are choosing the scope of consistency to suit your argument.\n\n\n- inside of entity-manager, your change is consistent\n- inside of openbmc, your change is inconsistent, e.g. `phosphor-logging` uses clear boundary for template var\n- inside of wider cpp community, your change is also inconsistent, considering template systems like `%s`, or `std::format`.\n\nentity-manager is not all stars and rainbows, we sadly cannot always use it's code as reference for how to write new code."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "Although there is no strict rule for defining template variables and developers are free to establish their own conventions with proper documentation, it is still recommended to follow established best practices. In that regard, I agree with using {} to denote template variables."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "closing this one, we can continue discussion on your markdown docs \ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank You!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I would expect SlotNumber to be \"PCIe SLOT 6\", there is no indication any function is applied to the property value."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "these numbers can be slot numbers/ instance numbers which can be used across other related dbus objects to have consistency in naming the fru's inv path or led obj path or temp sensor path or even redfish uri path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I like your base idea of being able to define a template var as part of a config file and then applying it inside the config file for consistency.\n\n\nIf i were to see `@DeviceName` anywhere in the config, i would expect it to be replaced with the exact contents of that property."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "| i would expect it to be replaced with the exact contents of that property.\n\nWe have already defined $ to be replaced with exact content. However, this replacement is not required in all scenarios.\n\nIn certain runtime scenarios, we may need to extract numeric values from the string instead of replacing them. These extracted numbers can then be interpreted at runtime as a slot number, instance number, or location code, depending on the context."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Ok, i may have misunderstood something about your change, i first thought that it only applied inside a single configuration record.\n\nIf it's just like the old `${bus}` template var system, and the only thing it does different is that it extracts the number then it's a different story.\n\nResolving this one for now."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "please add unit-tests for the feature"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "please add unit-tests for the feature"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyanga.ramasamy@dell.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "I've already added the unit test in commit message. Please check if you think anything else could be added."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Manual tests are nice but not sufficient for this kind of feature. Your feature can easily be unit-tested in similar to how it's done for the existing template var system\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/1f08ce74119b4cbd97e542e11eefc5fe99de9d94/test/entity_manager/test_entity-manager.cpp#L73"
                },
                {
